\section{Experimental Evaluation}
\label{sec:eval}

\textbf{Research Questions.}
\textbf{RQ1:} \emph{QoE--stall Pareto front} --- does the catastrophic-ratio knob $\rho_{\mathrm{cat}}$ trace a non-trivial Pareto front, and does the VMAF-aware fallback Pareto-dominate uniform-decrement projection at matched rebuffer budgets?
\textbf{RQ2:} \emph{Baseline competitiveness} --- where do the recommended operating points of the Pareto family sit relative to RobustMPC and Pensieve in the (QoE, Rebuffer) plane?
\textbf{RQ3:} \emph{Component ablations} --- isolated value of future-aware lookahead, Lyapunov-style cues, and Lagrangian dual updates inside the constrained policy.
\textbf{RQ4:} \emph{Shield-design space structure} --- across $\VShieldVariants$ shield variants, do behaviors collapse into a small number of equivalence classes, and which inference-time mechanisms add measurable headroom?
\textbf{RQ5:} \emph{Policy/shield co-design} --- to what extent do constrained-trained policies depend on having a shield available at inference?

\subsection{Experimental setup and datasets}

We evaluate on a multi-video trace-driven emulator (\(K_e{=}48\) chunks per episode, fixed segment duration \(T_{\mathrm{c}}\) as in Sec.~\ref{sec:system}).
\textbf{Primary suite (broadband-style).} FCC/Norway-style partitioned throughput traces consistent with public community releases~\cite{fcc2015mba,kvalbein2014} and the codebase evaluation paths; four videos \(\times\) twenty paired seeds per method after warmup.
\textbf{Stress suite (OOD).} Synthetic 5G/mmWave-style traces with intermittent LOS/NLOS segments and outage plateaus stress tail risk~\cite{meng2024mmwave}; Sec.~\ref{sec:eval:ood} reports paired replay of the \emph{same} constrained policy under identical harness assumptions.
Pensieve is reproduced with observation masking for fairness; RobustMPC follows~\cite{yin2015control}.
\textbf{Shield pairing protocol.} All legacy vs.\ VMAF-aware comparisons hold the trained policy, ladder, traces, and Video\(\times\)Episode identifiers fixed and vary only inference-time shield logic, enabling per-episode paired tests.
\textbf{Reporting integrity.} Genie~\cite{mao2017neural} uses non-causal trace knowledge and is an oracle reference only---not a deployable competitor for statistical dominance claims.

