\subsection{Statistical significance (paired shield vs.\ legacy)}

Means can hide heavy tails; paired nonparametric tests anchor claims about \emph{systematic} shifts on identical episodes.
Table~\ref{tab:wilcoxon:vmaf:legacy} summarizes Wilcoxon signed-rank outcomes for the recommended VMAF-aware operating point ($\tau{=}1.0$, budget 8) against legacy projection on $n{=}80$ paired traces.
\textbf{Result.} QoE and rebuffering improve with $p{<}0.01$; VMAF at $\tau{=}1.0$ is marginally significant ($p{=}0.056$), while tightening to $\tau{=}0.8$ yields a strictly significant triple at $\alpha{=}0.05$ (VMAF $p{=}0.041$, Table~\ref{tab:pareto:family}).

\begin{table}[t]
